#: ../../source/assy.rst:2
msgid "Assembly YAML"
msgstr "Assembly YAML"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:6
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "简介"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:8
msgid ""
"Assembly YAML is an approach to define assemblies using a simple YAML file. "
"This file format was introduced in PartCAD for the first time."
msgstr "Assembly YAML 是一种使用简单的 YAML 文件来定义装配体的方法。该文件格式在 PartCAD 中首次引入。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:13
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr "语法"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:15
msgid ""
"Each Assembly YAML (ASSY) file is a YAML file consisting of a tree of nodes."
" Each node is either a reference to an external part, a reference to an "
"external assembly, a reference to an external scene (in a scene only, see "
":ref:`assy-scenes`), or a container for such references."
msgstr ""
"每个 Assembly YAML（ASSY）文件都是一个由节点树构成的 YAML "
"文件。每个节点要么是对外部零件的引用，要么是对外部装配体的引用，要么是对外部场景的引用（仅在场景中，参见 :ref:`assy-scenes` "
"），要么是此类引用的容器。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:21
msgid "Containers"
msgstr "容器"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:23
msgid ""
"A container node is a node that holds other nodes rather than placing an "
"object. The container nodes have the following syntax:"
msgstr "容器节点是容纳其他节点、而不放置对象的节点。容器节点的语法如下："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:37
msgid ""
"The top-level node of an ASSY file is such a node, and it **is the "
"assembly**: what it holds is held by the assembly directly, not by anything "
"in between. So an assembly declared from a file whose root lists three parts"
" has three nodes in it and not one, and `location` on that root moves all "
"three - there is no node of its own for it to move instead. A `links:` list "
"*inside* the file is a node like any other: it is addressable by `name` from"
" a `map:`, and what it holds belongs to it."
msgstr ""
"ASSY 文件的顶层节点就是这样一个节点，而且它 **就是装配体本身** "
"：它所容纳的内容由装配体直接容纳，中间不经过任何其他层级。因此，由一个根节点列出了三个零件的文件所声明的装配体，其中有三个节点而不是一个，并且该根节点上的"
" `location` 会同时移动这三者——没有一个专属于它自己的节点可供移动。而写在文件 *内部* 的 `links:` "
"列表，则是与其他节点一样的节点：它可以从 `map:` 中通过 `name` 寻址，并且它所容纳的内容归它所有。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:47
msgid "What a link is called"
msgstr "链接的名称"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:49
msgid "Every link of an ASSY file has a name, and one rule gives it:"
msgstr "ASSY 文件的每个链接都有一个名称，并由同一条规则确定："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:51
msgid "its own ``name:``, where it gives one;"
msgstr "它自己的 ``name:`` ，如果给出了的话；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:52
msgid "otherwise the part or the assembly it places;"
msgstr "否则，是它所放置的零件或装配体的名称；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:53
msgid ""
"otherwise its position in the ``links:`` list it is written in, one-based, "
"as ``link#2``."
msgstr "否则，是它在所处的 ``links:`` 列表中的位置（从 1 开始计数），形如 ``link#2`` 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:56
msgid ""
"Only a ``links:`` container reaches the third -- a node that places "
"something is named after it -- and it exists so that there is no such thing "
"as a link that cannot be named. That one name is what everything uses: what "
"a ``connect:`` names as the link to connect to, what a ``map:`` names as a "
"node (joined with ``/`` for a path of them, ``head/head_half_1``), what a "
"connection's ``interferes:`` names, what a :ref:`filter <assy-filter>` "
"selects, and what the `PartCAD extension for VS Code "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_ shows as the row for that link in the viewer."
msgstr ""
"只有 ``links:`` "
"容器才会用到第三条——放置了某个对象的节点以该对象命名——它的存在是为了确保不存在无法命名的链接。这个唯一的名称正是各处所使用的： "
"``connect:`` 用它指明要连接到哪个链接， ``map:`` 用它指明某个节点（用 ``/`` 连接起来即构成一条由它们组成的路径，如 "
"``head/head_half_1`` ），连接的 ``interferes:`` 用它指名节点， :ref:`过滤器 <assy-filter>` "
"用它进行筛选，`面向 VS Code 的 PartCAD 扩展 "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_ 也用它作为查看器中该链接所在行的名称。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:65
msgid ""
"It is not the same thing as the *object* a link places, and the viewer shows"
" both: an assembly that places the same bolt a hundred times holds one "
"object under a hundred link names, and it is the link name that says which "
"of them this one is. So a position is used rather than the object's name "
"where there is nothing else -- a name shared by a hundred rows would say "
"nothing about any of them."
msgstr ""
"它与链接所放置的 *对象* "
"并不是一回事，而查看器会同时显示两者：一个把同一颗螺栓放置了一百次的装配体，持有的是一个对象、却对应着一百个链接名称，而正是链接名称说明了这一个究竟是其中的哪一个。因此，只有在没有其他依据时才使用位置、而不是对象的名称——一个被一百行共用的名称，对其中任何一行都说明不了什么。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:72
msgid ""
"Names need not be unique, though. A file that places four legs in a loop may"
" call every one of them ``leg``, and a name every leg answers to cannot pick"
" one of them out. So a :ref:`filter <assy-filter>` may also name **any** "
"link by its position, ``link#3``, whatever it is otherwise called -- the "
"IDE's 2D and Draft panels name a link that way exactly when its name is "
"shared with another link beside it."
msgstr ""
"不过，名称不必是唯一的。一个在循环中放置四条腿的文件可以把它们全都叫做 ``leg`` ，而四条腿都响应的同一个名称，无法把其中某一条单独挑出来。因此，"
" :ref:`过滤器 <assy-filter>` 也可以用位置来指名 **任何** 一个链接，即 ``link#3`` ，无论它本来叫什么——IDE "
"的 2D 和 Draft 面板，恰恰是在某个链接的名称与旁边另一个链接重名时，才以这种方式来称呼它。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:91
msgid ""
"A positional name is relative to the list it is written in, so adding a link"
" above one renames it. Name a container you intend to refer to."
msgstr "位置名称是相对于它所写入的那个列表而言的，因此在某个链接上方新增一个链接，就会改变它的名称。对于打算引用的容器，请为其命名。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:95
msgid "Parts"
msgstr "零件"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:97
msgid ""
"The following syntax is used to create a node that places a part in the "
"assembly:"
msgstr "以下语法用于创建一个将零件放入装配体的节点："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:133
msgid ""
"The `name` a node is given is how everything else in and around this "
"assembly refers to it: the `name` of a `connect`/`connectPorts` names a "
"node, and so does the first element of the `map:` section that decides which"
" of the ports inside this assembly the assembly itself has (see "
":ref:`assembly-ports`). A node with no `name` of its own is known by the "
"name of the part or assembly it places, which is enough until the same one "
"is placed twice."
msgstr ""
"赋予某个节点的 `name` ，是这个装配体内部及其周边的一切引用它的方式： `connect` / `connectPorts` 的 `name` "
"指名的是一个节点，决定该装配体本身拥有其内部哪些端口的 `map:` 一节，其第一个元素也是如此（参见 :ref:`assembly-ports` "
"）。没有自己 `name` 的节点，以它所放置的零件或装配体的名称为名，这在同一个对象被放置两次之前都是够用的。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:140
msgid ""
"One and only one method for placing the object is acceptable. Therefore the "
"sections `location`, `connectPorts` and `connect` are mutually exclusive. "
"Both `connectPorts` and `connect` are used to connect parts to each other by"
" matching their ports. `connect` is universal, while `connectPorts` is "
"specific to connecting with ports and without interface mating."
msgstr ""
"放置对象的方法有且仅有一种。因此 `location` 、 `connectPorts` 和 `connect` 这几个部分是互斥的。 "
"`connectPorts` 和 `connect` 都用于通过匹配零件的端口来将它们彼此连接。 `connect` 是通用的，而 "
"`connectPorts` 则专用于通过端口进行连接、且不涉及接口配合的场景。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:145
msgid ""
"The `with` and `to` fields are used to specify the names of interfaces. "
"Where `with` is the interface of the part that is getting added to the "
"assembly, and `to` is the interface of the part that is already in the "
"assembly. The `withInstance` and `toInstance` fields are used to specify the"
" names of interface instances. The `withPort` and `toPort` fields are used "
"to specify the names of ports."
msgstr ""
"`with` 和 `to` 字段用于指定接口的名称。其中 `with` 是正在被添加到装配体中的那个零件的接口，而 `to` "
"是已经存在于装配体中的那个零件的接口。 `withInstance` 和 `toInstance` 字段用于指定接口实例的名称。 `withPort` "
"和 `toPort` 字段用于指定端口的名称。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:151
msgid ""
"The `exploded` field does not affect the assembly itself: it is how far "
"apart the two parts are drawn in the exploded view of this step in the "
"assembly instruction book (`pc render -t pdf` and `pc render -t html`), and "
"in the assembly drawn whole with its `exploded` parameter set (see "
":doc:`config_objects`). Without it, the two are spaced by half of the "
"largest dimension of the two."
msgstr ""
"`exploded` 字段不影响装配体本身：它决定在装配说明书（`pc render -t pdf` 和 `pc render -t "
"html`）中此步骤的爆炸视图里两个零件相距多远，以及在设置了 `exploded` 参数而整体绘制的装配体中相距多远（参见 "
":doc:`config_objects`）。没有它时，两者之间的间隔为两者最大尺寸的一半。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:158
msgid ""
"An interface built from parameters is implemented under the name it was "
"built with - a post of one length implements "
"`//pub/std/imperial/dimensional-lumber:cuboid;x=88.9,y=743.7,z=88.9` - which"
" a connection to a post of any length cannot spell. So `with` and `to` may "
"name such an interface without its parameters, and stand for the one "
"parametrization of it that the part implements. A part that implements two "
"of them has to be told which, by name."
msgstr ""
"由参数构建出来的接口，是以构建它时所用的那个名称被实现的 - 某个特定长度的立柱实现的是 "
"`//pub/std/imperial/dimensional-lumber:cuboid;x=88.9,y=743.7,z=88.9` - "
"而一个要连到任意长度立柱上的连接写不出这个名称。所以 `with` 和 `to` "
"可以不带参数地指名这样的接口，用它来代表该零件所实现的那一种参数化形式。如果某个零件实现了其中两种，就必须按名称告诉它是哪一种。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:166
msgid ""
"`toParams` and `withParams` give values to the freedom-of-movement "
"parameters of the two interfaces (see :ref:`interface-parameters`), and both"
" are read in the **contact frame** - the frame where the two ports meet, "
"which is the port of the part being added (`with`), and the port of the part"
" it is added to (`to`) turned round to face it. So a `turnZ` in `toParams` "
"turns the part about the target port's Z axis *reversed*: `turnZ: 30` turns "
"it -30 degrees about the target port's own Z."
msgstr ""
"`toParams` 和 `withParams` 给这两个接口的运动自由度参数赋值（参见 :ref:`interface-parameters` "
"），而两者都是在 **接触坐标系** 中读取的 - 也就是两个端口相遇的那个坐标系，它由被添加零件的端口（ `with` "
"）以及它所添加到的那个零件的端口（ `to` ，转过来与之相对）构成。所以 `toParams` 中的 `turnZ` 会让该零件绕目标端口的 Z 轴 "
"*反向* 转动：`turnZ: 30` 会让它绕目标端口自身的 Z 轴转 -30 度。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:177
msgid "Joints"
msgstr "关节"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:179
msgid ""
"A connection is a **joint** when it keeps a degree of freedom once it is "
"made - a hinge, a slide, a bearing. Which of the two interfaces' parameters "
"stay free is declared in `motion:` (see :ref:`joints` for the whole of it), "
"on the interfaces, on the mating between them, and on the connection itself,"
" the most specific of which wins:"
msgstr ""
"当一个连接建立之后仍保留某个自由度时，它就是一个 **关节** - 铰链、滑动、轴承。两个接口的哪些参数保持自由，是在 `motion:` "
"中声明的（全部内容参见 :ref:`joints` ），可以声明在接口上、在它们之间的配合上，以及在连接本身上，其中最具体的那一个胜出："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:198
msgid ""
"`motion` takes everything an interface's `motion` takes. Its `axis` is in "
"the contact frame, where `toParams` are read too; `motion: fixed` locks a "
"joint the interfaces would let move, for one test or one variant of a "
"product."
msgstr ""
"`motion` 接受接口的 `motion` 所接受的一切。它的 `axis` 位于接触坐标系中，`toParams` "
"也是在那里读取的；`motion: fixed` 会把接口本来允许活动的关节锁死，用于某一次测试或某个产品变体。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:201
msgid ""
"`physics` is what moving the joint costs (damping, friction, effort and "
"velocity limits, a spring), and outranks the mating's and the interfaces'."
msgstr "`physics` 说的是让关节运动要付出什么代价（阻尼、摩擦、力与速度上限、一个弹簧），它优先于配合的和接口的。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:203
msgid ""
"`joint` names the joint: what a simulation reports it under, and what "
"another joint's `mimic` points at. It is not `name`, which is the link this "
"one is connected to. Without it the joint is `<this link>-<that link>` - "
"`upper_arm-base` above - and since link names need not be unique, a second "
"joint of one name is `<name>-2`, a third `<name>-3`, in link order, and `pc "
"test` asks for a `joint:` on each."
msgstr ""
"`joint` 给这个关节命名：仿真报告它时所用的名称，以及另一个关节的 `mimic` 所指向的名称。它不是 `name` "
"，后者指的是这条链接所连接到的那条链接。不写它时，关节就叫 `<this link>-<that link>` - 上面的例子里是 "
"`upper_arm-base` - 而由于链接名称不必唯一，同一名称的第二个关节叫 `<name>-2` ，第三个叫 `<name>-3` "
"，按链接顺序排，而 `pc test` 会要求每一个都写上 `joint:` 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:210
msgid ""
"`toParams` and `withParams` place the joint where it **starts**, and a "
"parameter at zero is the joint's zero. The assembly as drawn - rendered, "
"viewed, exported as geometry - is the mechanism at those values, exactly as "
"it always was; a parameter that is not a degree of freedom is what it always"
" was too, an adjustment fixed at its value."
msgstr ""
"`toParams` 和 `withParams` 把关节放到它 **开始** 时所处的位置，而参数取零就是关节的零点。画出来的装配体 - "
"渲染出来的、查看到的、作为几何导出的 - "
"就是处于那些取值下的那个机构，与一向的做法完全相同；而不是自由度的参数也和一向一样，是一次被固定在其取值上的调整。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:216
msgid ""
"A connection that keeps no degree of freedom attaches the part rigidly: "
"there are no fixed joints. A scene's connections make no joints at all - a "
"scene states where things are, and every element of one moves on its own. "
"Which parts are one rigid body, and which move against which, follows from "
"that: see :ref:`sim-bodies`."
msgstr ""
"不保留任何自由度的连接会把零件刚性地固连上去：不存在固定关节。场景的连接完全不形成关节 - "
"场景陈述的是各物体的位置，而它的每一个元素都自行运动。哪些零件属于同一个刚体、哪些相对哪些运动，都由此而来：参见 :ref:`sim-bodies` 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:222
msgid ""
"`pc info <assembly>` lists the joints under ``Joints``: the two links each "
"one joins, every degree of freedom it keeps - its kind, axis, range, "
"starting value, and which parameter and which declaration it came from - and"
" its physics."
msgstr ""
"`pc info <assembly>` 会在 ``Joints`` 下列出各个关节：每一个所接合的那两条链接、它所保留的每一个自由度 - "
"它的种类、轴线、取值范围、起始值，以及它来自哪个参数和哪一处声明 - 以及它的物理属性。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:226
msgid ""
"A link is placed once, against a link already placed, so a closed chain - a "
"four-bar linkage - cannot be *placed* by its connections: closing it takes a"
" connection whose target is placed after it, or a second placement of a link"
" already placed. Both are refused, and `pc test` says so. What closes the "
"chain is stated instead, as a further joint (see \"Further joints\" below)."
msgstr ""
"链接只被放置一次，而且是相对一条已经放置好的链接，所以闭合链 - 比如四连杆机构 - 无法由它的各个连接 *放置* "
"出来：要闭合它，就需要一个目标在它之后才被放置的连接，或者对一条已经放置好的链接再做一次放置。两者都会被拒绝，而 `pc test` "
"会如实说明。闭合这条链的东西要改用别的方式陈述，也就是作为一个额外的关节（见下文“Further joints”）。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:235
msgid "Further joints"
msgstr "额外的关节"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:237
msgid ""
"A link is placed by one connection, and many make more joints than that once"
" they are where it puts them. A rail placed against the left leg of a frame "
"meets the right leg too; a top placed on one leg rests on all four; anything"
" that closes a loop has a joint that no connection placed. "
"`alsoConnectPorts` states them, in the words of `connectPorts`:"
msgstr ""
"链接是由一个连接放置的，而许多链接一旦到了它所放到的位置，就会形成比那更多的关节。一根横梁靠在机架的左腿上，它同时也碰到了右腿；一块台面放在一条腿上，其实搁在四条腿上；任何闭合了回路的东西，都有一个不是由连接放置出来的关节。`alsoConnectPorts`"
" 就是用来陈述它们的，写法与 `connectPorts` 相同："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:254
msgid ""
"It places nothing. Once every link of the list is placed, the two ports have"
" to be in one place, facing each other - which is what makes a joint of them"
" - and `pc test` fails the assembly where they are not: a frame whose sizes "
"do not close the loop, or a port named on the wrong face. It is stated on "
"the later of the two links, once both are there, and the assembly "
"instruction book says so at the step that places it."
msgstr ""
"它什么都不放置。一旦列表中的每一条链接都被放置好，那两个端口就必须处在同一个位置并彼此相对 - 正是这一点让它们构成一个关节 - 而 `pc test`"
" "
"会让它们并非如此的装配体失败：比如一个尺寸无法闭合回路的机架，或者一个指名在错误面上的端口。它陈述在两条链接中较晚的那一条上，也就是两者都已到位之后，而装配说明书会在放置它的那一步把这件事说明出来。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:261
msgid ""
"A rigid assembly is all a further joint is checked for so far. A mechanism "
"with a closed chain - a four-bar linkage - states it the same way, and is "
"checked where it starts; a simulation does not yet hold it closed as it "
"moves (see docs/design/simulation.md, section 8.9)."
msgstr ""
"到目前为止，额外的关节只在刚性装配体上被检查。带闭合链的机构 - 比如四连杆机构 - "
"用同样的方式陈述它，并在它的起始状态被检查；而仿真目前还不会在它运动过程中保持它闭合（参见 docs/design/simulation.md 第 "
"8.9 节）。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:267
msgid "Expected overlaps"
msgstr "预期的重叠"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:269
msgid ""
"`pc test` checks that the parts of an assembly do not share space - except "
"where a joint says they must. A pin snapped into its hole, a screw cutting "
"its own thread: the joint is made by occupying the material, and a model "
"that holds no springs holds it overlapping. Two things say so, and both are "
"read from the joint, never declared against a pair of parts:"
msgstr ""
"`pc test` "
"会检查装配体中的各零件不占用同一空间——除非某个接合要求它们必须如此。卡入孔中的销钉、自行切出螺纹的螺钉：接合正是通过占据材料来实现的，而不含弹簧的模型只能以重叠的方式来保持它。有两样东西可以声明这一点，并且这两样都是从接合本身读取的，绝不是针对某一对零件来声明的："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:275
msgid ""
"the mating or the `how` of the connection says `snapIn` or `selfScrew`, or "
"an interface or a port it joins cuts its own way in (`selfScrew`). The "
"overlap expected is between the two parts that provide the joined ports - "
"followed through any `map:` of a sub-assembly to the part inside it that "
"provides the port;"
msgstr ""
"连接的配合或 `how` 声明了 `snapIn` 或 `selfScrew` ，或者它所接合的某个接口或端口会自行开路进入（ `selfScrew` "
"）。预期的重叠出现在提供所接合端口的那两个零件之间 - 并会沿着子装配体的任何 `map:` 一直追溯到其内部提供该端口的那个零件；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:280
msgid ""
"`interferes` lists the further nodes the same act of joining drives into: a "
"screw connected to the part its head bears on cuts its thread in the ones "
"underneath as well, and a sub-assembly fitted by one of its pins drives its "
"other pins into the same neighbour."
msgstr ""
"`interferes` "
"列出同一次接合动作还会挤入的其他节点：一颗螺钉连接到它的头部所抵靠的零件上时，也会在下方的那些零件中切出螺纹；而通过自身某一根销钉装配到位的子装配体，也会把它的其他销钉挤入同一个相邻件中。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:285
msgid ""
"`interferes` names nodes of the same `links:` list as the connection, by the"
" :ref:`name of the link <assy-link-names>`, which every link has: a node "
"inside a `links:` container is `container/name`, and a container that gave "
"itself no name is a level of that path like any other (`link#2/bracket`). A "
"node may be a part or an assembly. Naming an assembly excuses every overlap "
"between the two, which is as precise as the declaration is: a sub-assembly "
"with a mapped port is named rather than the part inside it that provides the"
" port, since it is the sub-assembly that is fitted."
msgstr ""
"`interferes` 通过每个链接都具备的 :ref:`链接名称 <assy-link-names>` ，指名与该连接处于同一个 `links:` "
"列表中的节点： `links:` 容器内部的节点写作 `container/name` ，而未给自己命名的容器也和其他层级一样，是该路径中的一级（ "
"`link#2/bracket` "
"）。节点可以是零件，也可以是装配体。指名一个装配体，会豁免两者之间的所有重叠，其精确程度就取决于这条声明本身：对于带有映射端口的子装配体，应当指名该子装配体，而不是其内部提供该端口的那个零件，因为被装配到位的是这个子装配体。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:294
msgid ""
"An assembly answers only for what it puts together. A sub-assembly declared "
"in `partcad.yaml` and placed in it has a verdict of its own, which the "
"assembly takes rather than repeats: only the overlaps between what it places"
" are looked at there, and every assembly - declared or a `links:` container "
"- is first compared by the box around everything in it."
msgstr ""
"装配体只对自己所组装的内容负责。在 `partcad.yaml` "
"中声明、并被放入其中的子装配体有自己的判定结果，装配体直接采纳该结果而不会重复判定：在那里只考察它所放置的各对象之间的重叠，并且每个装配体——无论是声明出来的还是一个"
" `links:` 容器——都先按包围其全部内容的盒体来比较。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:301
msgid "Assemblies"
msgstr "装配体"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:303
msgid ""
"The following syntax is used to create a node that places an assembly in the"
" assembly:"
msgstr "以下语法用于创建一个将装配体放入装配体的节点："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:310
msgid ""
"A scene places a scene the same way, with ``scene:``, and may mark what any "
"of its links places ``fixed:``; an assembly may do neither (see :ref:`assy-"
"scenes`)."
msgstr ""
"场景用 ``scene:`` 以同样的方式放置另一个场景，并且可以把它任何一条链接所放置的东西标记为 ``fixed:`` ；而装配体两者都不可以（参见"
" :ref:`assy-scenes` ）。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:314
msgid "Description"
msgstr "描述"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:316
msgid ""
"The `description` field of any node is free form text about that node: the "
"part or the assembly it places, or - on a container node - the sub-assembly "
"it declares."
msgstr ""
"任何节点的 `description` 字段都是关于该节点的自由格式文本：它所放置的零件或装配体，或者——在容器节点上——它所声明的子装配体。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:328
msgid ""
"It is used when the assembly is documented (`pc render -t pdf` and `pc "
"render -t html`): the description of the file's own root node is what the "
"assembly instruction book says about the assembly as a whole, unless the "
"package that declares the assembly gives it a `desc` of its own; the "
"description of a container node is what the book says about that sub-"
"assembly; and the description of a part or assembly node is shown with the "
"step that adds it, as the instruction for that step - the book composes a "
"sentence out of the connection only for a node that has no description, and "
"sets it apart, smaller, for one that does. The description of a fastener "
"that goes in at the step of the item it holds (see `pc render` in "
":doc:`/cli`) is shown at that step, once however many fasteners say the same"
" thing. Write it for whoever builds the thing: which faces meet, what is "
"flush, how far in, which way up. Nothing else in PartCAD parses it or acts "
"upon it."
msgstr ""
"它会在为装配体生成文档时使用（ `pc render -t pdf` 和 `pc render -t html` "
"）：文件自身根节点的描述，就是装配说明书中对整个装配体的说明，除非声明该装配体的包为它给出了自己的 `desc` "
"；容器节点的描述，是说明书中对那个子装配体的说明；而零件或装配体节点的描述，则与添加它的那个步骤一同显示，作为该步骤的说明 - "
"只有在节点没有描述时，说明书才会根据连接自己组一句话出来，而对有描述的节点，它会把那句话另行放在一旁、字号更小。在它所固定项目那一步一并装入的紧固件（参见"
" :doc:`/cli` 中的 `pc render` "
"）的描述，会在那一步显示，不论有多少个紧固件说的是同一件事，都只显示一次。写它的时候要面向实际动手装配的人：哪些面相接、什么要齐平、装进去多深、哪一面朝上。PartCAD"
" 中没有任何其他地方会解析它或据其行事。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:343
msgid "Comment"
msgstr "注释"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:345
msgid ""
"The `comment` field of a `connect` or `connectPorts` section is free form "
"text."
msgstr "`connect` 或 `connectPorts` 一节的 `comment` 字段是自由格式文本。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:354
msgid ""
"It is supplementary context for a human, or for an LLM, that is reading the "
"assembly. PartCAD never parses it and never acts upon it; it is shown as a "
"note beside the step this connection makes in the assembly instruction book,"
" and reported by `pc info`."
msgstr ""
"它是为阅读该装配体的人、或为 LLM 提供的补充背景信息。PartCAD "
"从不解析它，也从不据其行事；它会作为备注显示在装配说明书中该连接所对应的步骤旁边，并由 `pc info` 报告。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:361
msgid ""
"`comment` is **not** a place for assembly instructions. Everything that is "
"required to perform the assembly must be codified in the other ASSY fields, "
"so that the tools that consume the assembly - and not just the people "
"reading it - have the complete picture. Anything stated only in `comment` is"
" invisible to them."
msgstr ""
"`comment` **不是** 用来写装配说明的地方。执行装配所需的一切，都必须在其他 ASSY "
"字段中明确编码，这样一来，消费该装配体的工具——而不只是阅读它的人——才能掌握完整的信息。只写在 `comment` 中的内容，对它们是不可见的。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:368
msgid "How"
msgstr "How（装配方式）"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:370
msgid ""
"The `how` field of a `connect` or `connectPorts` section describes how the "
"object is expected to be brought into place. All of its fields are optional,"
" and so is the section itself: an omitted field means the default below."
msgstr ""
"`connect` 或 `connectPorts` 一节的 `how` "
"字段描述该对象预期以何种方式被安放到位。它的所有字段都是可选的，这一节本身也是可选的：省略某个字段即表示采用下面给出的默认值。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:396
msgid ""
"The units are SI, with the exception of lengths, which are in millimetres "
"like everywhere else in PartCAD:"
msgstr "单位采用国际单位制，长度除外——长度与 PartCAD 中其他各处一样，以毫米为单位："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:400
msgid "Field"
msgstr "字段"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:400
msgid "Quantity"
msgstr "物理量"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:400
msgid "Unit"
msgstr "单位"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:402
msgid "``pushForceMax``"
msgstr "``pushForceMax``"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:402 ../../source/assy.rst:410
msgid "force"
msgstr "力"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:402 ../../source/assy.rst:410
msgid "``N`` (newton)"
msgstr "``N`` （牛顿）"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:404
msgid "``pushDistance``"
msgstr "``pushDistance``"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:404 ../../source/assy.rst:408
msgid "length"
msgstr "长度"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:404 ../../source/assy.rst:408
msgid "``mm`` (millimetre)"
msgstr "``mm`` （毫米）"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:406
msgid "``turnTorqueMax``"
msgstr "``turnTorqueMax``"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:406
msgid "torque"
msgstr "力矩"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:406
msgid "``N*m`` (newton-metre)"
msgstr "``N*m`` （牛顿·米）"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:408
msgid "``threadStep``"
msgstr "``threadStep``"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:410
msgid "``hold*Force`` ``hold*ForceMin`` ``hold*ForceMax``"
msgstr "``hold*Force`` ``hold*ForceMin`` ``hold*ForceMax``"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:415
msgid ""
"Pushing an object into place is a linear motion, so ``pushForceMax`` bounds "
"a **force** in newtons. Turning it is a rotation, so ``turnTorqueMax`` "
"bounds a **torque** in newton-metres."
msgstr ""
"把对象推入到位是一种直线运动，因此 ``pushForceMax`` 限定的是以牛顿为单位的 **力** 。转动它则是一种旋转，因此 "
"``turnTorqueMax`` 限定的是以牛顿·米为单位的 **力矩** 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:421
msgid ""
"``pushForceMax`` was called ``pushTorqueMax`` in the first draft of this "
"section. The old spelling is still accepted, with a warning, and means the "
"same thing."
msgstr ""
"在本节的初稿中， ``pushForceMax`` 曾被称作 ``pushTorqueMax`` 。旧写法目前仍被接受（并伴随一条警告），含义完全相同。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:425
msgid ""
"`threadStep` is the **lead**: the axial distance the object advances per "
"full turn. For a multi-start thread that is the pitch multiplied by the "
"number of starts, not the pitch itself. When it is non-zero, the assembler "
"manages the pushing force and the turning torque together, so that the "
"resulting motion reproduces the given thread (or, more generally, rotation) "
"pattern, staying within `pushForceMax` and `turnTorqueMax`. The default of "
"`0.00` means a straight push with no turning."
msgstr ""
"`threadStep` 是 **导程** "
"：对象每转一整圈所前进的轴向距离。对于多头螺纹，它等于螺距乘以头数，而不是螺距本身。当它非零时，装配器会把推力和转动力矩放在一起管理，使最终的运动复现所给定的螺纹（更一般地说，是旋转）规律，并始终保持在"
" `pushForceMax` 和 `turnTorqueMax` 的范围之内。默认值 `0.00` 表示只做直线推入、不做转动。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:433
msgid ""
"A thread belongs to the interfaces rather than to any one connection, so it "
"is normally declared there and left out here - see :ref:`interface-thread` "
"below. Given on a connection, it overrides what the interfaces say for that "
"one step."
msgstr ""
"螺纹属于接口，而不属于某一个单独的连接，因此它通常在接口那里声明、在这里省略——参见下文的 :ref:`interface-thread` "
"。若在某个连接上给出了它，它会在那一个步骤中覆盖接口的说法。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:437
msgid ""
"`pushDirection` is not a field: it is deduced from the connection itself and"
" reported alongside the rest. It is the direction, in the assembly's "
"coordinates, that the object travels while it is pushed into place - so the "
"object starts at `pushDistance` back along it."
msgstr ""
"`pushDirection` "
"不是一个字段：它由连接本身推导得出，并与其余内容一同报告。它是在装配体坐标系中，对象被推入到位时所行进的方向——因此对象的起点就在沿该方向回退 "
"`pushDistance` 处。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:442
msgid ""
"The interfaces are what it is deduced from. The positive Z axis of an "
"interface points **into** the object the interface belongs to, which is "
"exactly the way a part coming to meet it has to travel. "
"`examples/feature_interface` shows this directly: both faces of the same 3mm"
" bracket are instances of one interface, the ``outer`` one at ``z=0`` "
"unrotated and the ``inner`` one at ``z=3`` turned around, so the two axes "
"point at each other through the material. Each of the four M3 screws in that"
" example is connected to one of those faces, and its deduced direction "
"points from the screw through the bracket towards the motor - reversing, as "
"it must, when the motor is placed on the other side."
msgstr ""
"推导的依据正是接口。接口的 Z 轴正方向指向该接口所属对象的 **内部** ，而这恰恰就是前来与之相接的零件必须行进的方向。 "
"`examples/feature_interface`  直接展示了这一点：同一块 3mm 支架的两个面都是同一个接口的实例， ``outer`` "
"那个位于 ``z=0`` 且未旋转， ``inner`` 那个位于 ``z=3`` 且被翻转过来，于是两条轴穿过材料彼此相对。该示例中的四颗 M3 "
"螺钉各自连接到其中一个面上，其推导出的方向从螺钉穿过支架指向电机——而当电机被放到另一侧时，这个方向也必然随之反向。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:452
msgid ""
"`pushDistance` is how far away from its final place the object starts: the "
"distance, along `pushDirection`, between the staging pose and the pose where"
" its `with` ports coincide with the target's `to` ports. When it is omitted,"
" it is derived from the object being connected, as **1.5 times that object's"
" own length along the Z axis of the interface location** it is connected by "
"- far enough for the object to clear the target before the insertion move "
"begins. That measurement needs the object's geometry, so it is made only "
"when something asks for it, never while the assembly is merely being "
"instantiated. If the geometry cannot be built at all, the distance is "
"reported as unset rather than guessed."
msgstr ""
"`pushDistance` 是对象的起点距其最终位置有多远：即沿 `pushDirection` 方向，预备位姿与其 `with` 端口和目标的 "
"`to` 端口重合时的位姿之间的距离。省略它时，该值由被连接的对象推导得出，取为 **该对象自身沿其所用接口位置的 Z 轴方向的长度的 1.5 倍** "
"——这足以让对象在插入动作开始之前与目标完全错开。这项测量需要对象的几何体，因此只有在有需求时才会进行，绝不会仅因为装配体被实例化就去做。如果几何体根本无法构建，该距离会报告为未设置，而不是去猜测。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:463
msgid ""
"`stage` names a group of steps that are expected to be connected **at the "
"same time** rather than one after another: consecutive nodes carrying the "
"same `stage` form one such group. It is a free-form label, so it can say "
"what the group is for. A `stage` that is interrupted by another one and then"
" resumes is reported, since the steps it names are then not consecutive and "
"will not be performed together."
msgstr ""
"`stage` 命名的是一组预期 **同时** 连接、而不是一个接一个连接的步骤：带有相同 `stage` "
"的连续节点构成这样的一组。它是自由格式的标签，因此可以说明这一组是做什么用的。如果某个 `stage` "
"被另一个打断之后又恢复，系统会报告这一情况，因为它所指的那些步骤此时并不连续，也就不会被同时执行。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:491
msgid ""
"`holdWith` names the interface of the object that is getting added to the "
"assembly, to be used to hold that object while it is connected. `holdTo` "
"names the interface of the object that is already in the assembly, which is "
"held the same way. Either may be a single interface name or a list of them. "
"An interface built from parameters is named with its values, as the object "
"implements it - `nail-grip;d=4.1148` - and however they are spelled: "
"`d=4.11480` names the same grip, and `m-thru;size=4,depth=3` the same "
"opening as `m-thru;depth=3,size=4`. The same holds for the `hold` field "
"below."
msgstr ""
"`holdWith` 指名正在被添加到装配体中的那个对象的接口，用于在连接过程中握持该对象。`holdTo` "
"指名已经存在于装配体中的那个对象的接口，它以同样的方式被握持。两者都可以是单个接口名称，也可以是一组接口名称的列表。由参数构建出来的接口是连同它的取值一起被指名的，就像对象实现它时那样"
" - `nail-grip;d=4.1148` - 而且无论怎么写都算：`d=4.11480` 指的是同一个 grip，而 "
"`m-thru;size=4,depth=3` 和 `m-thru;depth=3,size=4` 指的是同一个开口。下面的 `hold` "
"字段同样如此。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:516
msgid ""
"When `holdWith` is omitted, it defaults to the `hold` field of the `connect`"
" section of the part or the assembly being added (see :ref:`hold`). When "
"`holdTo` is omitted, it defaults to the `hold` field of the object being "
"connected to. When neither is set, the assembler is free to hold the object "
"however it sees fit."
msgstr ""
"省略 `holdWith` 时，它默认取被添加的零件或装配体的 `connect` 一节中的 `hold` 字段（参见 :ref:`hold` ）。省略"
" `holdTo` 时，它默认取被连接到的那个对象的 `hold` 字段。两者都未设置时，装配器可以按它认为合适的任何方式握持该对象。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:521
msgid ""
"`holdWithInstance` and `holdToInstance` select which instance of the "
"interface to hold by, for the cases where the object implements more than "
"one instance of it. They are matched positionally against `holdWith` and "
"`holdTo`. When omitted, the instance defaults to the `holdInstance` field of"
" that same section, and, failing that, to the first instance of the "
"interface."
msgstr ""
"`holdWithInstance` 和 `holdToInstance` "
"用于选择按接口的哪一个实例来握持，适用于对象实现了该接口的多个实例的情形。它们按位置与 `holdWith` 和 `holdTo` "
"相对应。省略时，实例默认取同一节中的 `holdInstance` 字段；若仍没有，则取该接口的第一个实例。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:527
msgid ""
"`holdWithForceMin` and `holdWithForceMax` bound the force each end is held "
"with, in newtons - enough to keep the object from moving, not so much as to "
"damage it. `holdWithForce` sets both at once, and `holdToForce*` are the "
"same for the object being connected to. Each bound is resolved on its own, "
"from the first of these that gives it:"
msgstr ""
"`holdWithForceMin` 和 `holdWithForceMax` "
"限定握持每一端所用的力，单位为牛顿——足以让对象不发生移动，又不至于损坏它。 `holdWithForce` 一次性设置两者，而 "
"`holdToForce*` 对被连接到的那个对象起同样的作用。每个边界值各自独立解析，取下列来源中第一个给出它的："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:533
msgid "the bound itself, `holdWithForceMin` or `holdWithForceMax`;"
msgstr "边界值本身，即 `holdWithForceMin` 或 `holdWithForceMax` ；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:534
msgid "`holdWithForce`, which sets both;"
msgstr "`holdWithForce` ，它同时设置两者；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:535
msgid ""
"the `holdForceMin`/`holdForceMax` field of the `connect` section of the part"
" or the assembly (see :ref:`hold`);"
msgstr ""
"零件或装配体的 `connect` 一节中的 `holdForceMin` / `holdForceMax` 字段（参见 :ref:`hold` ）；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:537
msgid "the `holdForce` field of that same section, which sets both;"
msgstr "同一节中的 `holdForce` 字段，它同时设置两者；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:538
msgid "the defaults, **3 N** for the minimum and **7 N** for the maximum."
msgstr "默认值，最小值为 **3 N** ，最大值为 **7 N** 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:540
msgid ""
"A minimum that ends up above its maximum is a contradiction rather than a "
"range: it is reported, and both bounds fall back to the defaults."
msgstr "最终高于其最大值的最小值是一个矛盾，而不是一个区间：这会被报告，并且两个边界值都回退到默认值。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:546
msgid "The thread of an interface"
msgstr "接口的螺纹"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:548
msgid ""
"An interface may declare the thread that connections made through it advance"
" along, and whether it cuts its own:"
msgstr "接口可以声明：通过它建立的连接沿着怎样的螺纹前进，以及它是否自行切出螺纹："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:559
msgid ""
"Both are inherited by the interfaces that inherit this one, so a thread is "
"spelled out once, on the interface that introduces it. In "
"`examples/feature_interface` the abstract `m3` interface carries `0.5` and "
"the abstract `m4` carries `0.7` - the real pitches of those screws - and "
"every opening, screw and hole pattern derived from them connects with the "
"right thread without repeating it."
msgstr ""
"这两项都会被继承该接口的那些接口所继承，因此螺纹只需在引入它的那个接口上写明一次。在 `examples/feature_interface` "
"中，抽象接口 `m3` 带有 `0.5` ，抽象接口 `m4` 带有 `0.7` "
"——即这些螺钉的真实螺距——而由它们派生出的每一个开口、螺钉和孔位阵列，都无需重复声明就能以正确的螺纹进行连接。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:566
msgid ""
"A connection inherits `threadStep` from the two interfaces it mates. They "
"have to agree on it: two different threads cannot be screwed together, and a"
" connection whose ends disagree is reported and fails ``pc test``. Unless, "
"that is, one of them declares `selfScrew` - a self-tapping screw, or the "
"plain hole one goes into. Then the thread of the end that does have to match"
" one is the thread that gets cut, and failing that the one the self-tapping "
"end brings with it."
msgstr ""
"连接会从它所配合的两个接口继承 `threadStep` 。两者必须在这一点上一致：两种不同的螺纹无法拧在一起，两端不一致的连接会被报告，并使 ``pc"
" test`` 失败。除非其中一端声明了 `selfScrew` "
"——比如自攻螺钉，或者它所拧入的普通光孔。这时，确实必须与之匹配的那一端的螺纹，就是被切出来的那个螺纹；若没有这样的一端，则采用自攻的那一端自身带来的螺纹。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:574
msgid "A port may say `selfScrew` of itself:"
msgstr "端口可以就它自己声明 `selfScrew` ："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:584
msgid ""
"It says what the interface's says, for every joint made through that port - "
"and it is what a connection naming the port alone (`withPort:`, "
"`connectPorts:`) goes by, since such a connection looks up neither interface"
" nor their mating. Every copy of the port keeps it: the `tip` of each part "
"that implements `nail-point`, and the port an assembly's `map:` makes of it."
msgstr ""
"它说的就是该接口所说的内容，对通过那个端口建立的每一个关节都生效 - 而且对于只指名端口的连接（ `withPort:` 、 "
"`connectPorts:` ），它也正是所依据的东西，因为这样的连接既不去查接口、也不去查它们之间的配合。该端口的每一个副本都保留它：每一个实现了 "
"`nail-point` 的零件的 `tip` ，以及某个装配体的 `map:` 由它做出来的那个端口。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:591
msgid "How a mating goes together"
msgstr "配合是如何装到一起的"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:593
msgid ""
"A pair of interfaces that always goes together the same way - an M3 screw "
"into an M3 tapped hole, a clip onto its rail - says so once, in a ``how`` "
"section of its mating, instead of on every connection:"
msgstr ""
"总是以同一种方式装到一起的一对接口——M3 螺钉拧入 M3 攻丝孔、卡扣扣上它的导轨——只需在其配合的 ``how`` "
"一节中声明一次，而不必在每个连接上都写一遍："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:614
msgid ""
"It takes the fields of a connection's ``how`` that say how the object goes "
"in: ``pushForceMax``, ``pushDistance``, ``turnDirection``, "
"``turnTorqueMax``, ``threadStep``, ``selfScrew`` and ``snapIn``. ``stage`` "
"is not one of them - which steps are done together is the assembly's to say "
"- and nor are the ``hold*`` fields, which belong to the objects (see "
":ref:`hold`)."
msgstr ""
"它接受连接的 ``how`` 中那些说明对象如何进入的字段： ``pushForceMax`` 、 ``pushDistance`` 、 "
"``turnDirection`` 、 ``turnTorqueMax`` 、 ``threadStep`` 、 ``selfScrew`` 和 "
"``snapIn`` 。 ``stage`` 不在其中——哪些步骤一起完成由装配体来决定—— ``hold*`` 这些字段也不在其中，它们属于对象（参见"
" :ref:`hold` ）。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:620
msgid ""
"Every connection made through the pair gets them, and an ASSY file overrides"
" them **field by field**: a step whose own ``how`` gives only "
"``turnTorqueMax`` keeps the mating's thread and direction. The order, most "
"specific first, is the connection's ``how``, the mating's ``how``, the "
"mating's own ``selfScrew`` and ``snapIn``, the interfaces' ``threadStep`` "
"and ``selfScrew`` and the ports' ``selfScrew``, and the defaults."
msgstr ""
"通过这一对接口建立的每个连接都会获得这些设置，而 ASSY 文件会 **逐个字段地** 覆盖它们：一个自身的 ``how`` 只给出了 "
"``turnTorqueMax`` 的步骤，仍然保留配合所给的螺纹和方向。按从最具体到最一般的顺序依次是：连接的 ``how`` 、配合的 "
"``how`` 、配合自身的 ``selfScrew`` 和 ``snapIn`` 、接口的 ``threadStep`` 和 "
"``selfScrew`` 以及端口的 ``selfScrew`` ，最后是默认值。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:628
msgid "Reading the instructions back"
msgstr "回读装配说明"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:630
msgid ""
"Everything resolved from the sections above - the inherited threads, the "
"deduced push direction, the forces each end is held with - is reported by"
msgstr "由上述各节解析得出的一切——继承而来的螺纹、推导出的推入方向、握持每一端所用的力——都会由以下命令报告"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:637
msgid ""
"under ``Connections``, one entry per connected object. That is the "
"assembly's own account of how it is built, for a person or for whatever "
"performs it."
msgstr ""
"报告位于 ``Connections`` "
"之下，每个被连接的对象对应一条记录。这就是装配体对自己如何被装配出来的说明，既供人阅读，也供执行装配的任何一方使用。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:641
msgid "Testing the instructions"
msgstr "测试装配说明"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:643
msgid ""
"Everything above is resolved leniently: a field that is missing takes its "
"default, and one that contradicts itself is reported and replaced with a "
"default, so that an assembly always builds. ``pc test`` is what looks past "
"that leniency. Its ``connect`` test fails an assembly whose instructions had"
" to be repaired to be usable, and passes one that is sound - **including one"
" that says nothing at all** and takes every default."
msgstr ""
"上面的一切都是宽松解析的：缺失的字段取其默认值，自相矛盾的字段会被报告并替换为默认值，这样装配体总能构建出来。 ``pc test`` "
"正是越过这种宽松去审视的那一环。它的 ``connect`` 测试会让那些必须经过修复才可用的装配说明不通过，而让本身就健全的装配说明通过—— "
"**包括什么都没说、全部采用默认值的那种** 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:650
msgid "What it rejects today:"
msgstr "它目前会拒绝的情况："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:652
msgid ""
"a ``*Min`` above its corresponding ``*Max`` - ``holdWithForceMin`` above "
"``holdWithForceMax``, or ``holdToForceMin`` above ``holdToForceMax``. A "
"minimum above a maximum is a contradiction rather than a range."
msgstr ""
"某个 ``*Min`` 高于与之对应的 ``*Max`` —— ``holdWithForceMin`` 高于 ``holdWithForceMax``"
" ，或者 ``holdToForceMin`` 高于 ``holdToForceMax`` 。高于最大值的最小值是一个矛盾，而不是一个区间。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:655
msgid ""
"two interfaces that disagree about their `threadStep` with neither declaring"
" `selfScrew`."
msgstr "两个接口的 `threadStep` 不一致，而且两者都没有声明 `selfScrew` 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:657
msgid ""
"a `motion:` that contradicts itself - a `type` and a `dof` that describe "
"different degrees of freedom (the `type` is the short form of the `dof`, so "
"beside one it is an assertion about it), a `fixed` motion with a `dof`, "
"`limits` that bound a parameter declared with a different range, a range on "
"one of a `ball`'s turns (a ball is bounded by one angle) - on the "
"interfaces, the mating or the connection."
msgstr ""
"`motion:` 自相矛盾 - 一个 `type` 和一个 `dof` 描述的是不同的自由度（ `type` 是 `dof` "
"的简写形式，所以与后者并列时它就是关于后者的一个断言）、一个 `fixed` 运动却带着 `dof` 、`limits` "
"限定了一个以不同取值范围声明的参数、给 `ball` 的某一个转动加了取值范围（球关节由一个角度统一限定）- 无论它写在接口、配合还是连接上。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:663
msgid "a `dof` naming no freedom-of-movement parameter."
msgstr "`dof` 指名了一个并非运动自由度参数的东西。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:664
msgid ""
"a joint that starts outside its own bounds - a `toParams` beyond the range "
"of the parameter it sets. `limits` on a *target* interface are stated about "
"its port's Z, which is the contact frame's Z reversed, so they bound the "
"target's `turnZ` the other way round: `limits: {lower: -10, upper: 30}` with"
" `toParams: {turnZ: 20}` starts it outside, at 20 of -30 to 10."
msgstr ""
"关节的起始位置落在它自己的限位之外 - 也就是某个 `toParams` 超出了它所设定参数的取值范围。*目标* 接口上的 `limits` "
"是按它端口的 Z 轴陈述的，而那是接触坐标系 Z 轴的反向，所以它们对目标的 `turnZ` 的限定是反过来的：`limits: {lower: "
"-10, upper: 30}` 配上 `toParams: {turnZ: 20}` 就会让它从界外开始，在 -30 到 10 的范围里取了 20。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:669
msgid ""
"two interfaces stating different `physics` for the joint they make together,"
" when the mating states none (see :ref:`joints`)."
msgstr "两个接口对它们共同构成的那个关节陈述了不同的 `physics` ，而配合又什么都没陈述（参见 :ref:`joints` ）。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:671
msgid "two joints of one name (see \"Joints\" above)."
msgstr "两个关节同名（见上文“Joints”）。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:672
msgid "a screw motion with no `threadStep` to advance by."
msgstr "一个螺纹运动却没有可供推进的 `threadStep` 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:673
msgid ""
"a connection that would close a loop, or that places a link already placed."
msgstr "一个会闭合回路的连接，或者一个去放置已经放置过的链接的连接。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:675
msgid ""
"It is `pc test` rather than `pc lint` because each of these is a finding "
"about what a connection *resolved* to: which interfaces and which mating it "
"matched, which parameters they inherit from other packages, which ones a "
"`motion:` brought along. `pc lint` checks a file as it is written, and "
"caches its verdict on that file - a verdict about interfaces declared in "
"another package would go stale there the moment that package changed. `pc "
"test` keys its verdict on the assembly, whose key covers the interfaces it "
"connects."
msgstr ""
"之所以是 `pc test` 而不是 `pc lint` ，是因为上面每一条都是关于某个连接 *解析* "
"成了什么的发现：它匹配上了哪些接口和哪一个配合、它们从其他包继承了哪些参数、某个 `motion:` 又带来了哪些参数。`pc lint` "
"检查的是文件写下来的样子，并把它的结论按那个文件来缓存 - 而一个关于另一个包中所声明接口的结论，在那个包一变就会在那里过期。`pc test` "
"则把它的结论按装配体来做键，而装配体的键涵盖了它所连接的那些接口。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:688
msgid "Steps that can be followed"
msgstr "可以照着做的步骤"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:690
msgid ""
"Defaults are enough for an assembly to build, and they are not enough for a "
"person to put it together. So an assembly that is meant to be made "
"(``manufacturable: true``) is held to more by ``pc test``: every item after "
"the first of each list of links has to be connected (``connect`` or "
"``connectPorts``), and something has to say **how** it goes into place - "
"pushed, snapped or screwed in. That is said by any of:"
msgstr ""
"默认值足以让装配体构建出来，却不足以让人把它装配起来。因此，对于打算真正制造出来的装配体（ ``manufacturable: true`` ）， "
"``pc test`` 的要求更高：每个链接列表中第一项之后的每一项都必须是连接起来的（ ``connect`` 或 ``connectPorts`` "
"），并且必须有某处说明它 **以何种方式** 被安放到位——是推入、卡入还是拧入。下列任何一处都可以说明这一点："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:697
msgid ""
"the connection's own ``how``, with at least one of ``pushForceMax``, "
"``pushDistance``, ``turnDirection``, ``turnTorqueMax``, ``threadStep``, "
"``selfScrew`` or ``snapIn`` (``stage`` and the ``hold*`` fields say when and"
" by what, not how);"
msgstr ""
"连接自身的 ``how`` ，其中至少给出 ``pushForceMax`` 、 ``pushDistance`` 、 "
"``turnDirection`` 、 ``turnTorqueMax`` 、 ``threadStep`` 、 ``selfScrew`` 或 "
"``snapIn`` 之一（ ``stage`` 和 ``hold*`` 这些字段说明的是何时以及用什么来做，而不是以何种方式）；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:701
msgid ""
"the mating of the two interfaces it connects through: any field of its "
"``how`` (see \"How a mating goes together\" above), or its own ``snapIn`` or"
" ``selfScrew``, which then says it for every connection that pairs them;"
msgstr ""
"它所通过的那两个接口之间的配合：该配合的 ``how`` 的任意字段（参见上文“配合是如何装到一起的”），或者配合自身的 ``snapIn`` 或 "
"``selfScrew`` ——这样一来，凡是把这两个接口配成一对的连接都得到了说明；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:704
msgid ""
"the interfaces themselves, with a ``threadStep`` or ``selfScrew``, or the "
"ports that meet, with a ``selfScrew``: a thread is screwed in, and a way cut"
" in is driven."
msgstr ""
"接口本身，带有 ``threadStep`` 或 ``selfScrew`` ；或者相遇的那两个端口，带有 ``selfScrew`` "
"：有螺纹就要拧入，而有自行开出的通路就要压入。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:708
msgid ""
"The ``manufacturability`` test reports each step that says none of these; an"
" item placed by ``location:`` is the ``connectivity`` test's to report. The "
"IDE's Build vs Buy table shows an assembly with such steps as "
"**Incomplete**, listing them, until they are fixed."
msgstr ""
"``manufacturability`` 测试会报告每一个这些都没有说明的步骤；而由 ``location:`` 放置的项，则交由 "
"``connectivity`` 测试来报告。在这些步骤被修正之前，IDE 的 Build vs Buy 表格会把含有此类步骤的装配体显示为 "
"**Incomplete** ，并把它们逐一列出。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:716
msgid "Holding an object"
msgstr "握持对象"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:718
msgid ""
"The defaults for the `how` fields above are declared once, next to the part "
"or the assembly itself, in `partcad.yaml`:"
msgstr "上述 `how` 字段的默认值，只需在 `partcad.yaml` 中、紧挨着零件或装配体本身声明一次："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:739
msgid ""
"Everything an object contributes to every connection it takes part in lives "
"in that one `connect` section, rather than among the fields that describe "
"the object itself."
msgstr "一个对象为它所参与的每一个连接所贡献的全部内容，都放在那一个 `connect` 一节里，而不是混在描述该对象本身的那些字段之中。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:747
msgid "Scenes"
msgstr "场景"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:749
msgid ""
"The same file format defines a **scene**: a placed arrangement of objects, "
"such as a workcell, a table with parts laid out on it, or a simulation "
"world. A package declares one by pointing at the file from its ``scenes:`` "
"section rather than its ``assemblies:`` section (see :ref:`scenes`); there "
"is no assembly object in between, and nothing about the file itself says "
"which it is."
msgstr ""
"同一种文件格式也用来定义 **场景** ：一组摆放好的对象，比如一个工作单元、一张摆放着零件的桌子，或者一个仿真世界。包通过从它的 "
"``scenes:`` 一节、而不是 ``assemblies:`` 一节指向该文件来声明一个场景（参见 :ref:`scenes` "
"）；中间不存在装配体对象，并且文件本身没有任何地方说明它究竟是哪一种。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:761
msgid ""
"Everything above applies, but for one thing it may not say: **a scene may "
"not use** ``how``. An assembly is a product and says how it is put together,"
" which is what the assembly instruction book is generated from. A scene "
"states only an end state, and nothing in it was assembled, so there is "
"nothing to say about the assembling. Declaring ``how`` in a scene is an "
"error, both while the scene is being built and in the editor."
msgstr ""
"上面的一切都同样适用，只有一件事它不可以说：**场景不得使用** ``how`` "
"。装配体是一件产品，它说明自己是如何装配起来的，装配说明书正是据此生成的。而场景只陈述一个最终状态，其中没有任何东西是被装配出来的，因此也就无从谈起装配过程。在场景中声明"
" ``how`` 是一个错误，构建场景时和在编辑器中都是如此。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:768
msgid ""
"The ``connect`` and ``connectPorts`` sections themselves stay. Placing a "
"gripper against the fixture it holds is a statement about where things are, "
"and saying it with the ports the two objects declare is better than saying "
"it with coordinates somebody worked out by hand. They place; they do not "
"attach, and a connection that keeps a degree of freedom makes no joint in a "
"scene."
msgstr ""
"``connect`` 和 ``connectPorts`` "
"这两节本身仍然保留。把夹爪放到它所夹持的夹具上，陈述的是各物体所处的位置，而用这两个对象所声明的端口来表述它，要好过用某个人手工算出来的坐标。它们只放置；它们不固连，而在场景中，保留了自由度的连接也不形成任何关节。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:774
msgid ""
"Two things a scene may say that an assembly may not, and both follow from "
"the same difference -- everything in an assembly is attached to it, and "
"every element of a scene is a rigid body of its own (see :ref:`sim-bodies`):"
msgstr ""
"有两件事是场景可以说而装配体不可以说的，两者都源自同一个差别 -- 装配体中的一切都固连在它身上，而场景的每一个元素都各自是一个刚体（参见 "
":ref:`sim-bodies` ）："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:784
msgid ""
"``scene:`` places another scene. Every element of it is a body of its own in"
" turn, as every element of this one is. An assembly cannot hold one: a "
"product is not made of arrangements, and an assembly that tried would be "
"attached and loose at once. It is refused while the assembly is built, and "
"in the editor."
msgstr ""
"``scene:`` "
"放置另一个场景。它的每一个元素又各自是一个刚体，就像本场景的每一个元素一样。装配体装不下场景：产品不是由摆放构成的，而一个试图这样做的装配体会同时既是固连的又是松散的。构建该装配体时它会被拒绝，在编辑器中也会。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:788
msgid ""
"``fixed: true`` welds what the link places to the world -- a table, a tank's"
" walls, a robot bolted to the floor -- where otherwise it would fall. On a "
"link that places an assembly it welds that assembly's root body, and the "
"joints inside it still move; on a link that places a scene, or on a "
"``links:`` list, it fixes every element inside. In an assembly it is "
"reported and ignored: everything there is attached to the assembly already. "
"Only a ``true`` or a ``false`` is read, and it is not taken from the file's "
"top-level node, which is the scene itself: whether a scene is fixed is said "
"by whatever places it."
msgstr ""
"``fixed: true`` 把该链接所放置的东西焊接到世界上 -- 一张桌子、一个水池的池壁、一台用螺栓固定在地面上的机器人 -- "
"否则它就会掉下去。写在放置某个装配体的链接上时，它焊接的是那个装配体的根刚体，而它内部的各个关节仍然可以运动；写在放置某个场景的链接上、或者写在一个 "
"``links:`` 列表上时，它会固定其中的每一个元素。在装配体中它会被报告并忽略：那里的一切本来就已经固连在该装配体上了。只有 ``true`` 或"
" ``false`` 会被读取，而它不会取自文件的顶层节点（那就是场景本身）：一个场景是否被固定，由放置它的那一方来说明。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:819
msgid "Part of an assembly"
msgstr "装配体的一部分"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:821
msgid ""
"A sub-assembly worth looking at on its own is often not an object of its "
"own: the head of the logo, one bay of a rack, the parts that arrive in one "
"box. A **filter** names the links to keep and leaves the rest out."
msgstr ""
"值得单独查看的子装配体，往往并不是一个独立的对象：标志的头部、机架的某一格、装在同一个箱子里送来的那些零件。 **过滤器** "
"指名要保留哪些链接，并把其余的排除在外。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:825
msgid ""
"A filter is a tree of link names mirroring the tree the ASSY file already "
"is:"
msgstr "过滤器是一棵由链接名称构成的树，它与 ASSY 文件本身的那棵树相对应："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:833
msgid "Three rules, and nothing else:"
msgstr "只有三条规则，再无其他："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:835
msgid ""
"a link the filter names is kept, and a link it does not name is dropped;"
msgstr "过滤器指名的链接予以保留，它未指名的链接则被丢弃；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:836
msgid "a link named with nothing under it keeps everything under it;"
msgstr "被指名、但其下没有写任何内容的链接，保留它下面的全部内容；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:837
msgid ""
"a link named with at least one child under it keeps those children and drops"
" its other ones."
msgstr "被指名、且其下至少写了一个子节点的链接，保留这些子节点，并丢弃它的其他子节点。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:840
msgid ""
"A link is named the way :ref:`everything else names it <assy-link-names>`: "
"its ``name:``, the part or the assembly it places, or its position in its "
"``links:`` list. So there is no link a filter cannot name."
msgstr ""
"链接的指名方式与 :ref:`其他各处指名它的方式 <assy-link-names>` 相同：它的 ``name:`` "
"、它所放置的零件或装配体，或者它在所属 ``links:`` 列表中的位置。因此，不存在过滤器无法指名的链接。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:844
msgid ""
"A filter may equally be written as a list, which is the convenient form when"
" nothing below the names matters:"
msgstr "过滤器同样可以写成一个列表；当名称之下的内容都无关紧要时，这是更方便的写法："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:852
msgid "There are three ways to use one, and they do different things."
msgstr "过滤器有三种用法，它们所做的事情各不相同。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:855
msgid "Filtering for one picture"
msgstr "为某一张图进行过滤"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:857
msgid ""
"``pc render`` and ``pc export`` take ``--filter``, and write nothing into "
"the package: the assembly is built as it always is and the filter is applied"
" to the result, for this one file."
msgstr ""
"``pc render`` 和 ``pc export`` 接受 ``--filter`` "
"，并且不会向包中写入任何内容：装配体照常构建，过滤器只作用于构建结果，且仅针对这一个文件。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:867
msgid ""
"The argument is a **filename first**: a file somebody keeps beside the "
"package and edits. Only when there is no such file is the text read as the "
"filter itself, as JSON or YAML -- which is the convenient form for one link "
"and for whatever a script composes. A name that is neither is refused, "
"naming both things that went wrong, so a mistyped filename is not quietly "
"read as a link name."
msgstr ""
"该参数 **首先被当作文件名** ：一个有人保存在包旁边并加以编辑的文件。只有在不存在这样的文件时，这段文本才会被当作过滤器本身、按 JSON 或 "
"YAML "
"来读取——对于只有一个链接的情形，以及脚本临时拼出来的内容，这是更方便的写法。两者都不是的名称会被拒绝，并同时指出两方面的问题，这样拼错的文件名就不会被悄悄当成链接名称。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:874
msgid ""
"Everything kept stays where the whole assembly put it. A filter never re-"
"resolves a ``connect:``, which is the only reading of \"part of this "
"assembly\" that is true of the thing on the bench. Because the result is "
"built rather than written, a filter here may also select *inside* a link "
"that places an assembly of another package."
msgstr ""
"保留下来的一切都停留在整个装配体为它安排的位置上。过滤器绝不会重新解析 ``connect:`` "
"——对于工作台上的实物而言，这是“这个装配体的一部分”唯一成立的理解方式。由于这里的结果是构建出来的、而不是写出来的，因此这里的过滤器也可以在放置了另一个包的装配体的那个链接"
" *内部* 进行选择。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:880
msgid ""
"The same options are available in the `PartCAD extension for VS Code "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_: the **2D** and **Draft** tabs of the viewer list what the "
"object is made of beside the drawing, with a checkbox on every item, and "
"what is ticked is the filter the render is made with. On the 2D tab the list"
" also holds each node's ports and interfaces, and ticking one draws that "
"port on the projection -- the same thing ``--with-ports``, ``--with-"
"interfaces`` and ``--port`` ask for. All three Design tabs share one "
"selection, so what is ticked on the 3D view is what the 2D and Draft tabs "
"draw, and a box cleared on one is cleared on the others."
msgstr ""
"`面向 VS Code 的 PartCAD 扩展 "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_ 中也提供了同样的选项：查看器的 **2D** 和 **Draft** "
"标签页会在图形旁边列出该对象由什么构成，每一项都带一个复选框，被勾选的内容就是本次渲染所使用的过滤器。在 2D "
"标签页上，该列表还包含每个节点的端口和接口，勾选其中之一就会把那个端口画到投影上——这与 ``--with-ports`` 、 ``--with-"
"interfaces`` 和 ``--port`` 所要求的是同一件事。三个 Design 标签页共享同一份选择，因此在 3D 视图上勾选的内容，就是 "
"2D 和 Draft 标签页所绘制的内容，在其中一个上取消勾选，另外两个上也随之取消。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:891
msgid "Filtering every time the file is written"
msgstr "每次写出文件时都进行过滤"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:893
msgid ""
"A ``filter:`` on a ``render:`` or ``export:`` file type says the same thing "
"permanently, so a package can keep a picture of one sub-assembly checked in "
"beside the drawing of the whole of it. It is declared per file type, in "
"either place a file type is configured -- the package's own section, and the"
" object's:"
msgstr ""
"在 ``render:`` 或 ``export:`` 文件类型上写一个 ``filter:`` "
"，就把同样的意思永久地固定下来，于是一个包可以在整体图形旁边同时签入某个子装配体的图片。它按文件类型声明，可以写在配置文件类型的任一处——包自己的那一节，以及对象的那一节："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:916
msgid ""
"``pc render --filter`` and ``pc export --filter`` override it for one run, "
"the way ``--view`` overrides a configured viewport. A part and a sketch have"
" no links, so a filter over one of them is reported rather than ignored."
msgstr ""
"``pc render --filter`` 和 ``pc export --filter`` 会在单次运行中覆盖它，就像 ``--view`` "
"覆盖已配置的视口那样。零件和草图没有链接，因此对它们使用过滤器会被报告出来，而不是被忽略。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:921
msgid "Filtering into a new object"
msgstr "过滤成一个新对象"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:923
msgid ""
"``pc filter`` writes a declaration instead: the ASSY file of ``SRC`` with "
"everything the filter drops taken out of it, as ``DST.assy``, declared "
"beside ``SRC``."
msgstr ""
"``pc filter`` 则是写出一份声明：把 ``SRC`` 的 ASSY 文件中被过滤器丢弃的内容全部去掉，写成 ``DST.assy`` "
"，并声明在 ``SRC`` 旁边。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:932
msgid ""
"``DST`` is then an object like any other: it renders, it exports, it has a "
"bill of materials, suppliers quote for it, and it is a file somebody can "
"review as a diff. If ``SRC`` is an assembly then ``DST`` is an assembly, and"
" if ``SRC`` is a scene then ``DST`` is a scene -- the kind follows the "
"source. An existing ``DST`` is overwritten; its declaration is left alone "
"when it already points at the same file, so whatever file types were "
"configured for it survive a re-run."
msgstr ""
"此后 ``DST`` "
"就是一个与其他对象别无二致的对象：它可以渲染、可以导出、有物料清单、供应商可以为它报价，而且它是一个可供人以差异形式审阅的文件。如果 ``SRC`` "
"是装配体，那么 ``DST`` 也是装配体；如果 ``SRC`` 是场景，那么 ``DST`` 也是场景——类别随源而定。已存在的 ``DST`` "
"会被覆盖；当它的声明已经指向同一个文件时，该声明保持不变，因此为它配置过的文件类型在重新运行后依然存在。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:939
msgid ""
"The **file** is filtered rather than the built assembly, which is what makes"
" the result an assembly somebody can build: every link kept keeps its "
"``connect:``, its ``how:``, its parameters and its comments. (That is also "
"why ``pc filter`` needs an Assembly YAML file to work from. A ``step`` or "
"``urdf`` assembly has no links of its own, and ``pc convert assembly -t "
"assy`` is what turns one into a file that does.) The one thing it cannot do "
"is select inside a link that places a part or another package's assembly; it"
" says so and keeps that link whole."
msgstr ""
"被过滤的是 **文件** ，而不是构建出来的装配体，正是这一点使得结果仍然是一个有人能够实际装配出来的装配体：保留下来的每个链接都保留了它的 "
"``connect:`` 、 ``how:`` 、参数和注释。（这也是 ``pc filter`` 需要有一个 Assembly YAML "
"文件可供处理的原因。 ``step`` 或 ``urdf`` 类型的装配体没有自己的链接，而 ``pc convert assembly -t "
"assy`` "
"正是把这样的装配体转换成带链接的文件的办法。）它唯一做不到的，是在放置了零件、或放置了另一个包的装配体的链接内部进行选择；它会说明这一点，并把该链接整体保留。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:947
msgid ""
"A link whose name was its position has that position **written into** the "
"copy as a ``name:``. Filtering moves links -- the second of five is the "
"first of two once the one above it has gone -- so a position would otherwise"
" rename it, and anything that named it would point at nothing."
msgstr ""
"名称原本就是其位置的链接，该位置会作为 ``name:`` **写入** "
"副本之中。过滤会使链接发生移动——五个之中的第二个，在它上面那个被去掉之后就成了两个之中的第一个——否则位置就会改变它的名称，而任何指名它的地方都将指向不存在的东西。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:952
msgid ""
"What filtering can break is exactly one thing, and it is checked: **a link "
"that is kept may be connected to a link that was dropped**. ``pc filter`` "
"reports every one of them, naming the line, and so does :ref:`pc lint <assy-"
"lint>` over the file afterwards."
msgstr ""
"过滤可能破坏的恰恰只有一件事，而且这件事是会被检查的： **保留下来的链接可能连接到了被丢弃的链接上** 。 ``pc filter`` "
"会逐一报告这类情况并指出所在行，事后对该文件运行 :ref:`pc lint <assy-lint>` 也会如此。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:961
msgid ""
"Name those links in the filter too, or place the kept ones with "
"``location:``."
msgstr "要么在过滤器中把那些链接也一并指名，要么用 ``location:`` 来放置保留下来的链接。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:967
msgid "Validation"
msgstr "校验"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:969
msgid ""
"ASSY files are checked against a JSON schema "
"(``src/partcad_utils/schema/assy.json``) that describes the document *after*"
" Jinja2 rendering: the node keys above, the shape of an OCCT location, and "
"the fact that ``location``, ``connectPorts`` and ``connect`` -- or ``part``,"
" ``assembly``, ``scene`` and ``links`` -- exclude one another."
msgstr ""
"ASSY 文件会依据一份 JSON 模式（ ``src/partcad_utils/schema/assy.json`` ）进行检查，该模式描述的是 "
"Jinja2 渲染 *之后* 的文档：上文列出的那些节点键、OCCT 位置的形式，以及 ``location`` 、 ``connectPorts`` "
"和 ``connect`` -- 或者 ``part`` 、 ``assembly`` 、 ``scene`` 和 ``links`` -- "
"彼此互斥这一事实。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:975
msgid ""
"One thing is checked beside the schema, because no schema can describe it: a"
" ``connect:``/``connectPorts:`` names a link of the **same** ``links:`` "
"list, written **above** this node, since that is where PartCAD looks for it "
"as the assembly is built. So does every name in a connection's "
"``interferes:``, which may be anywhere in the file. A name that is wrong "
"would otherwise be answered, much later, with \"Target part not found\" and "
"a part at the origin."
msgstr ""
"除该模式之外还有一项检查，因为没有任何模式能够描述它： ``connect:`` / ``connectPorts:`` 指名的必须是 **同一个** "
"``links:`` 列表中、写在本节点 **上方** 的链接，因为在构建装配体时 PartCAD 正是到那里去寻找它的。连接的 "
"``interferes:`` 中的每一个名称也同样如此，只不过它们可以位于文件中的任何地方。否则，一个写错的名称要等到很久以后，才会以“Target "
"part not found”和一个位于原点的零件作为回应。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:982
msgid ""
"A file read as a **scene** is checked against that schema with ``how`` "
"forbidden, and one read as an **assembly** with ``scene`` and ``fixed`` "
"forbidden. Both are derived from the one schema rather than kept beside it, "
"so the two cannot drift apart; only those rules differ."
msgstr ""
"被当作 **场景** 读取的文件，会依据那份模式进行检查，只是其中禁用了 ``how`` ；而被当作 **装配体** 读取的文件，则禁用 "
"``scene`` 和 ``fixed`` 。两者都是由那一份模式派生出来的，而不是与它并列单独维护，因此两者不会逐渐走样；差别只有这些规则。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:987
msgid ""
"Because the file on disk is a template rather than the YAML it renders to, "
"the checker **renders it** first, the way PartCAD does: with the parameters "
"its declaration in ``partcad.yaml`` gives it, at their defaults, as "
"``param_<name>``. What is checked is what that renders to -- the items a "
"loop produces, the branch an ``{% if %}`` takes, the numbers expressions "
"come to -- and every finding is reported at the line and column of the "
"template it came from: literal text at itself, a computed value at its ``{{ "
"}}``, every pass of a loop at the loop's body. A template that fails to "
"render with those values (an undefined name, or a deliberate call to an "
"undefined function to stop with a message) is reported on the line it failed"
" on, since PartCAD would stop there too."
msgstr ""
"由于磁盘上的文件是一个模板，而不是它所渲染出的那份 YAML，检查器会先像 PartCAD 那样 **把它渲染出来**：用它在 "
"``partcad.yaml`` 中的声明给它的那些参数，取各自的默认值，以 ``param_<name>`` 的形式传入。被检查的就是渲染出来的结果 "
"-- 循环所产生的那些条目、``{% if %}`` 所走的那个分支、各表达式算出的那些数字 -- "
"而每一条发现都报告在它所出自模板的行号和列号上：字面文本报告在它自己的位置，计算出来的值报告在它的 ``{{ }}`` "
"处，循环的每一轮都报告在循环体上。如果模板用那些取值渲染失败（比如出现未定义的名称，或者有意调用一个未定义的函数来带着消息中止），就报告在它失败的那一行上，因为"
" PartCAD 也会在那里中止。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:999
msgid ""
"A file no package declares has no known parameters, so it is checked masked "
"instead: ``{{ expr }}`` becomes a placeholder value and ``{% tag %}`` "
"becomes blanks of the same size. An expression alone on its line -- a macro "
"call, say -- stands for lines of YAML rather than a value, so it becomes "
"blanks too, as do the bodies of ``{% macro %}``, ``{% call %}`` and a block "
"``{% set %}``. Anything the mask makes unknowable -- what an expression "
"evaluates to, which branch of an ``{% if %}`` is taken -- is left unreported"
" rather than guessed at."
msgstr ""
"没有任何包声明过的文件，其参数无从得知，所以它改为按遮蔽方式检查：``{{ expr }}`` 变成一个占位值，``{% tag %}`` "
"变成同样长度的空白。单独占一行的表达式 -- 比如一次宏调用 -- 代表的是若干行 YAML 而不是一个值，所以它也变成空白，``{% macro "
"%}`` 、 ``{% call %}`` 以及块形式 ``{% set %}`` 的主体同样如此。凡是遮蔽之后无从得知的东西 -- "
"表达式求值的结果、``{% if %}`` 走的是哪一个分支 -- 都不予报告，而不是去猜测。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1008
msgid "What is to be made"
msgstr "什么是要被制造出来的"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1010
msgid ""
"An assembly marked ``manufacturable: true`` -- on its declaration, or on its"
" package or a package above it -- is held to more. Somebody has to "
"physically put it together, and a coordinate says where a part ends up but "
"not what holds it there. So no item of any ``links:`` list may have a "
"``location:``, and every item after the first has to say what it is joined "
"to with ``connect:`` or ``connectPorts:``; the first item of a list is the "
"one the others hang from. The document's own top-level ``location:`` beside "
"its ``links:`` -- the frame the whole assembly sits in -- is allowed; a file"
" that is a single ``part:`` or ``assembly:`` with no ``links:`` is that one "
"item, and may not. This is the rule ``pc test`` holds a manufacturable "
"assembly to (the ``connectivity`` test), reported where it is written, and "
"like that test it stands down for an assembly whose declaration says "
"``connectivity:`` with ``requireAnchored: false`` or ``skip: true``."
msgstr ""
"被标记为 ``manufacturable: true`` 的装配体 -- 标记在它的声明上，或者在它所在的包、或者它上面某个包上 -- "
"要受到更多约束。得有人实际把它装起来，而坐标只说明某个零件最终落在哪里，却没说明是什么把它固定在那里。所以任何 ``links:`` "
"列表中的任何条目都不得带 ``location:`` ，而第一项之后的每一项都必须用 ``connect:`` 或 ``connectPorts:`` "
"说明它与什么接合；列表的第一项就是其余各项所挂靠的那一个。文档自身与它的 ``links:`` 并列的顶层 ``location:`` -- "
"也就是整个装配体所处的那个坐标系 -- 是允许的；而一个只有一个 ``part:`` 或 ``assembly:`` 、没有 ``links:`` "
"的文件本身就是那一个条目，因此不得带它。这正是 ``pc test`` 用来约束可制造装配体的那条规则（也就是 ``connectivity`` "
"测试），它会在被写下的位置报告出来；而且与那项测试一样，如果某个装配体的声明在 ``connectivity:`` 中写了 "
"``requireAnchored: false`` 或 ``skip: true`` ，它就不再生效。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1024
msgid ""
"The same goes for a ``partcad.yaml``: a part marked manufacturable (on the "
"part, on the package, or on a package above it) that is not an ``alias`` or "
"an ``enrich`` has to say how it is had -- a ``manufacturing:`` section to "
"make it, or both a ``vendor:`` and an ``sku:`` to buy it."
msgstr ""
"``partcad.yaml`` 也是同样的道理：一个被标记为可制造（标记在零件上、在包上，或者在它上面某个包上）、而又不是 ``alias`` 或 "
"``enrich`` 的零件，必须说明它是怎么得到的 -- 要么有一个 ``manufacturing:`` 小节用来制造它，要么同时有 "
"``vendor:`` 和 ``sku:`` 用来采购它。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1029
msgid ""
"Both are errors, and both apply only to what is *marked*. PartCAD takes an "
"object as manufacturable unless something says otherwise, but a package "
"nobody has said that about is one still being sketched, and underlining all "
"of it would be underlining work in progress. ``pc init`` asks."
msgstr ""
"两者都是错误，而且都只适用于被 *标记过* 的东西。除非有东西另行说明，PartCAD "
"会把对象当作可制造的；但一个谁都没就此说过话的包，是一个还在打草稿的包，而把它整个都画上下划线，等于给进行中的工作画下划线。``pc init`` "
"会询问这一点。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1034
msgid "Run the checks over a package from the command line with:"
msgstr "在命令行中对整个包运行这些检查："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1040
msgid "or narrow it to ASSY files only:"
msgstr "或者把范围收窄到只检查 ASSY 文件："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1046
msgid ""
"To check individual files instead, name them. This runs in the ``pc`` "
"process itself -- no daemon, no package to load -- so it answers even when "
"the package does not:"
msgstr ""
"若要改为检查单个文件，把它们的名字写出来即可。这会在 ``pc`` "
"进程自身中运行——不需要守护进程，也不需要加载包——因此即便包本身给不出答案，它也依然能够作答："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1054
msgid ""
"Add ``--json`` for machine-readable findings (zero-based line and column "
"numbers), and ``--stdin`` to check content that has not been saved, which is"
" how an editor checks the buffer on screen:"
msgstr ""
"加上 ``--json`` 可得到机器可读的检查结果（行号和列号从 0 开始计数），加上 ``--stdin`` "
"可检查尚未保存的内容——编辑器正是以这种方式检查屏幕上的缓冲区："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1062
msgid ""
"Whether a single file is checked as an assembly or as a scene is not "
"something the file says, so ``pc lint --file`` works it out from the "
"``partcad.yaml`` files around it: a file at least one scene declares and no "
"assembly declares is a scene, and a file no package declares is checked as "
"an assembly -- so a scene nobody has declared yet is told its ``scene:`` and"
" ``fixed:`` are an assembly's mistake, with the advice to declare it under "
"``scenes:``. Say so outright with ``--schema``:"
msgstr ""
"单个文件究竟按装配体还是按场景来检查，文件本身并没有说明，因此 ``pc lint --file`` 会从它周围的那些 ``partcad.yaml``"
" 文件推断出来：如果至少有一个场景声明了某个文件、并且没有任何装配体声明它，那么它就是场景；而没有任何包声明过的文件则按装配体来检查 -- "
"于是一个还没人声明过的场景会被告知它的 ``scene:`` 和 ``fixed:`` 是装配体里的错误，并附上建议：把它声明到 ``scenes:``"
" 下面。用 ``--schema`` 可以直接把话说明白："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1074
msgid ""
"The same ``partcad.yaml`` files say what the file is rendered with: the "
"defaults of the parameters its declaration gives it, overridden -- exactly "
"as for every other ``pc`` command -- by the ``parameters:`` of "
"``~/.partcad/config.yaml`` and by ``--extra-param "
"<object>.<parameter>=<value>`` -- the object's name may have dots of its "
"own, and the value is read as the type the parameter declares. Without the "
"package's name to hand, an override may name the object with its package or "
"without it. ``--include-path`` adds a directory to include from, for an "
"``includePaths`` that a package importing this one from elsewhere declares:"
msgstr ""
"同样那些 ``partcad.yaml`` 文件也说明了该文件是用什么渲染出来的：它的声明给它的那些参数的默认值，并且 -- 与其他每一条 ``pc``"
" 命令完全一样 -- 会被 ``~/.partcad/config.yaml`` 的 ``parameters:`` 以及 ``--extra-"
"param <object>.<parameter>=<value>`` 覆盖 -- "
"对象的名称里本身可以带点，而取值按该参数所声明的类型来读取。在手头没有包名称时，覆盖项可以带包名指名该对象，也可以不带。``--include-"
"path`` 会增加一个用于包含的目录，以应对从别处导入本包的那个包所声明的 ``includePaths`` ："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1088
msgid ""
"The `PartCAD extension for VS Code "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_ runs exactly that while an ASSY file is open and shows the "
"findings in the Problems view. It answers the same question from the package"
" contents it has already loaded, which is the declaration itself rather than"
" a guess at it, and falls back to the command's own answer for a file no "
"loaded package mentions. Set ``partcad.lint.enabled`` to ``false`` to turn "
"that off."
msgstr ""
"`面向 VS Code 的 PartCAD 扩展 "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_ 在 ASSY 文件打开时运行的正是这项检查，并把检查结果显示在 Problems "
"视图中。它根据自己已经加载的包内容来回答同一个问题，那就是声明本身、而不是对声明的猜测；对于没有任何已加载的包提及的文件，它会回退到该命令自己给出的答案。把"
" ``partcad.lint.enabled`` 设为 ``false`` 即可关闭这项功能。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:1095
msgid ""
"``partcad.yaml`` is checked the same way, by the same checker, against the "
"configuration schema (``src/partcad_utils/schema/partcad.json``) -- see "
":doc:`/config_package`. It is a Jinja2 template too, so it is rendered "
"before it is checked exactly as an ASSY file is, and it has no "
"assembly/scene flavor: nothing points at a package configuration, so "
"``--schema`` does not apply to one."
msgstr ""
"``partcad.yaml`` 由同一个检查器以同样的方式、依据配置模式（ "
"``src/partcad_utils/schema/partcad.json`` ）进行检查 -- 参见 :doc:`/config_package`"
" 。它同样是一个 Jinja2 模板，因此会像 ASSY 文件那样在检查之前先被渲染出来；而且它没有装配体／场景之分：没有任何东西会指向一份包配置，所以"
" ``--schema`` 对它并不适用。"

